      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Weavertown, the settlement expanded in the early 1800s thanks to a thriving tanning industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/wevertown_new_york",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A tannery opened in 1833, and the hamlet was also known at times as Nobles Corners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wevertown%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "When the railroad reached the area in 1871, North Creek quickly became the transportation hub for the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
